  partName: Cylinder Head (2)
  description: The Cylinder Head (2) is a tiny, thin-flat component located at the
    middle-center-rear of the engine, constructed from metal-bright material. Its
    primary function is to seal the cylinders, facilitating efficient combustion
    and engine performance. Notably, the cylinder head's small size and thin-flat
    shape allow for precise control over combustion chamber geometry, enabling optimized
    engine performance, fuel efficiency, and emissions reduction.
